# Own-wording Tome of Heroes spells, chunk F (Outmaneuver to Rive). TEXT = {name: text}.
TEXT = {
"Outmaneuver": "When a creature provokes an opportunity attack from an ally you can see within range, you can force it to make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure its movement is reduced to 0, and you can move up to your speed toward it without provoking opportunity attacks. The spell does not interrupt your ally's opportunity attack, which happens before this spell's effects.",
"Oversized Paws": "The hands and feet of one willing creature within range become oversized and stronger. Until the spell ends, it adds 1d4 to the damage of its unarmed strikes.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Pierce the Veil": "You sketch a shimmering, ethereal doorway in the air and knock three times, calling an otherworldly entity to give insight or advice. The door swings open and the entity, wreathed in shadow or otherwise obscured, appears at the threshold. It answers up to five questions truthfully and as well as it can, though not always clearly or directly. It cannot pass through the doorway or interact with anything on your side except by speaking. Likewise, creatures on your side cannot pass through or interact with the other side except by asking questions. You and the creature understand each other's words even without a shared language, as under comprehend languages. When you cast the spell, you must request a specific named entity, a specific type of creature, or a creature from a specific plane. The creature cannot be native to the plane you are on. Then make an ability check with your spellcasting ability. The DC is 12 for a creature from a specific plane, 16 for a specific type of creature, or 20 for a specific entity. If the check fails, the responder is any entity of the GM's choosing, from any plane. In every case the creature has Intelligence of at least 8 and can speak and hear.",
"Pincer": "You force your enemies into a tight spot. Choose two points you can see within range, at least 30 feet apart. Each point emits a thunderous boom in a 30-foot cone aimed toward the other point, audible to 300 feet. Each creature in a cone makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failure it takes 5d10 Thunder damage and is pushed up to 10 feet from the point that emitted the cone. On a success it takes half damage and is not pushed. Objects in each cone that are not worn or carried are automatically pushed.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 6th.",
"Piper's Lure": "You touch a nonmagical pipe or horn and imbue it with a magic that lures creatures to it. Each creature that enters or starts its turn within 150 feet of the object makes a Wisdom saving throw or is Charmed for 10 minutes. A creature Charmed this way must Dash toward the object by the safest route on each of its turns. Once within 5 feet of it, the creature is also Incapacitated, staring and swaying to a mesmerizing tune only it hears. If the object is moved, the creature tries to follow. Every 10 minutes the creature repeats the save, ending the spell on it on a success. If the creature is attacked, the spell ends on it at once. A creature that has been Charmed by this spell cannot be Charmed by it again for 24 hours.",
"Portal Jaunt": "You touch a specially prepared key to a door or gate, making it a one-way portal to another door within range. It works with any crafted door, doorway, archway or other artificial opening, but not natural or accidental openings like cave mouths or wall cracks. You must know your destination or see it from where you cast. When you finish casting, the touched door opens and shows a shimmering image of the place beyond the destination door. You can move through and emerge instantly from the destination door, or let one other willing creature pass instead. Anything you carry, including other creatures, willing or not, goes with you. For the duration, locks, bars and magical effects such as arcane lock do nothing to the spell. You can only go to a side of the door you can see or have physically visited (divination such as clairvoyance counts as seeing). Once you or a willing creature passes through, both doors shut and the spell ends. If no one passes through within 1 round, it ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The range increases by 100 feet and the duration by 1 round for each slot level above 3rd. Each added round lets one more creature pass through before the spell ends.",
"Portal Trap": "You create a magical portal on a surface in a free space you can see within range. It covers up to 5 square feet and is at once hidden by an illusion. The illusion looks like the surrounding terrain or surface, such as mortared stone on a stone wall, or a simple image of your choice like one made by minor illusion. A creature that touches, steps on, or otherwise interacts with or enters the portal makes a Wisdom saving throw or is teleported to a free space up to 30 feet away in a random direction (roll a d8). It cannot be teleported into a solid object. Physically touching the illusion reveals it, but that triggers the portal. A creature that uses an action to examine the area can see the illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can create one more portal for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Power Word Fling": "You mutter a word of power that flings a creature you can see within range up or sideways. It makes a Strength saving throw or is thrown up to 15 feet vertically or horizontally. If it hits a surface such as a ceiling or wall, it stops and takes 3d6 Bludgeoning damage. If thrown vertically, it then falls, taking fall damage as normal unless it can fly or otherwise stop a fall. If it hits a creature, it stops and takes 3d6 Bludgeoning damage, and that creature makes a Strength saving throw or is knocked Prone. After being thrown sideways, or after falling from a vertical throw, the target is knocked Prone whether or not it hit anything. As a bonus action on each of your later turns, you can try to fling the same creature again, and it makes another Strength save or is thrown.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The fling distance grows by 5 feet and the impact damage by 1d6 for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Power Word Rend": "You speak a word of power that ruptures the internal organs of a creature you can see within range. It makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 4d6 + 20 Force damage on a failure or half on a success. If it is below half its hit point maximum, it has Disadvantage on this save. The spell has no effect on creatures without vital organs, such as constructs, oozes and undead.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 4th, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Protection from the Void": "Until the spell ends, one willing creature you touch has Resistance to Necrotic and Psychic damage and Advantage on saves against Void spells.",
"Reaper's Knell": "As a bell rings, a burst of necrotic energy ripples out in a 20-foot-radius sphere from a point you can see within range. Each creature in the area makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure it is marked with necrotic energy for the duration. If a marked creature drops to 0 hit points or dies before the spell ends, you regain hit points equal to 2d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier. Or you can choose one ally you can see within range to regain them instead.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The healing increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 4th.",
"Rebounding Bolt": "You fire a vibrant blue beam at a creature you can see within range. It then bounces to a creature of your choice within 30 feet of that target, losing vibrancy, and keeps bouncing to other creatures of your choice until it sputters out. Each later target must be within 30 feet of the previous one, and the beam cannot bounce to a target it already hit. Each target makes a Constitution saving throw. The first takes 5d6 Force damage on a failure, or half on a success. Each later target takes 1d6 less than the one before (4d6, then 3d6, 2d6, 1d6), down to 1d6 for the last, with half on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3rd. This lets the beam jump one more time, losing 1d6 on each bounce as normal.",
"Reciprocating Portal": "With a gesture and a muttered word, you open an inky black circular portal on the ground beneath one or more creatures. You can create one 15-foot-diameter portal, two 10-foot-diameter portals, or six 5-foot-diameter portals. A creature standing where a portal opens makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure it falls through, vanishes into a demiplane where it is Stunned as it falls endlessly, and the portal closes. At the start of your next turn, creatures that failed fall through matching portals directly above where they were. A falling creature lands Prone in its former space or the nearest free space and takes damage as if it fell 6d6, whatever the distance between the exit portal and the ground. Creatures that fly or are under levitate cannot be affected.",
"Reposition": "You designate up to three friendly creatures within range, one of which can be you. Each target teleports to a free space it chooses and can see within 30 feet of itself.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more friendly creature for each slot level above 4th.",
"Repulsing Wall": "You create a shimmering wall of light on a solid surface within range, up to 60 feet long, 20 feet high and 1 foot thick, or a ring up to 20 feet across, 20 feet high and 1 foot thick. It is translucent, and creatures have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to look through it. One side, chosen when you cast, deals 5d8 Radiant damage when a creature enters the wall for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there. A creature trying to pass through makes a Strength saving throw, and on a failure is pushed 10 feet from the wall and knocked Prone. An undead, a fiend, or a creature Vulnerable to Radiant damage has Disadvantage on this save. The other side deals no damage and does not restrict movement.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 4th.",
"Reset": "Choose up to four creatures within range. An ally can reroll Initiative and keep whichever result it prefers. An enemy makes a Wisdom saving throw or rerolls Initiative, keeping whichever result you prefer. Changes to the Initiative order take effect at the start of the next round.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can affect one more creature for each slot level above 4th.",
"Retribution": "You wrap yourself in shimmering ethereal armor. The next time a creature hits you with a melee attack, it takes Force damage equal to half the damage it dealt to you and makes a Strength saving throw. On a failure it is pushed up to 5 feet from you. Then the spell ends.",
"Rive": "You pull on the filaments of transition and possibility to tear at your enemies. Choose a creature you can see within range and make a ranged spell attack. On a hit it takes 5d8 Cold damage as strands of icy nothingness whip from your hand to envelop it. If it is not native to your plane, it also takes 3d6 Psychic damage and makes a Constitution saving throw or is Stunned until the end of its next turn.",
}
